{"book":"PSA","chapter":98,"source":"hbo","verses":[1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8,9],"records":[{"id":"PSA.98.1.s1","verses":[1],"source":"מִזְמ֡וֹרשִׁ֤ירוּ לַֽיהוָ֨ה׀שִׁ֣יר חָ֭דָשׁ כִּֽי־נִפְלָא֣וֹת עָשָׂ֑ה הוֹשִֽׁיעָה־לּ֥וֹ יְ֝מִינ֗וֹ וּזְר֥וֹעַ קָדְשֽׁוֹ׃","gloss":"A psalm. Sing to YHWH a new song, for wonders he has done; his right hand and his holy arm have won victory for him.","pieces":[[1,"A psalm. \\q Sing {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} a new song because of the wonders {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has done! \\q By {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} own right hand and {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} holy arm {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has won the victory.",null]],"L":{"1":"A psalm. \\q Sing to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} a new song, for {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has done wonders; \\q {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} right hand and {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} holy arm have won victory for {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}."},"R":{"1":"A song. \\q Sing a new song to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, because {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has done amazing things! \\q With {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} own power and holy strength {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has won the victory."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"punctuation","tokens":["o190980010011"],"choice":"The title shares verse 1","alternatives":[],"reason":"This psalm's title is one word, \"A psalm\", and the Hebrew counts it together with the first line as verse 1, so here the verse numbers are the same as in Bibles that print the title without a number.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190980010011"],"choice":"psalm: a song sung to music","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (mizmor) is a song sung with instruments. It is the only psalm in Psalms 93-99 with a title.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"idiom","tokens":["o190980010091","o190980010102","o190980010111","o190980010122"],"choice":"his right hand and holy arm have won victory for him: he won by his own power","alternatives":[],"reason":"The hand and arm stand for strength. God won the victory alone, with no one to help (Isaiah 59:16; 63:5), as at the sea (Exodus 15:6). The verb (hoshia') is \"save, give victory\".","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m4","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o190980010041","o190980010051"],"choice":"Psalm 96:1","alternatives":[],"reason":"The psalm opens like Psalm 96 and ends like it (98:9 and 96:13).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190980010111","o190980010122"],"choice":"his own power and holy strength","alternatives":["his right hand and his holy arm"],"reason":"Readable says what the hand and arm stand for (m3).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":"Creation greets its coming Judge","status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.98.2.s1","verses":[2],"source":"הוֹדִ֣יעַ יְ֭הוָה יְשׁוּעָת֑וֹ לְעֵינֵ֥י הַ֝גּוֹיִ֗ם גִּלָּ֥ה צִדְקָתֽוֹ׃","gloss":"YHWH has made known his salvation; before [the] eyes of the nations he has revealed his righteousness.","pieces":[[2,"{{divine_name:The LORD|Yahweh}} has let {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} saving power be known; \\q {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has shown {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} justice openly for the nations to see.",null]],"L":{"2":"{{divine_name:The LORD|Yahweh}} has made known {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} salvation; \\q before the eyes of the nations {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has revealed {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} righteousness."},"R":{"2":"{{divine_name:The LORD|Yahweh}} has shown everyone how {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} saves. \\q He has let the nations see that {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} does what is right."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190980020031","o190980020071"],"choice":"salvation, righteousness: God's saving justice","alternatives":[],"reason":"The two words (yeshu'ah, tsedaqah) are paired as in Isaiah 46:13 and 51:5-6: God puts things right by rescuing his people, and the nations see it.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o190980020042","o190980020052"],"choice":"Isaiah 52:10","alternatives":[],"reason":"Verses 2-3 echo Isaiah 52:10, where the LORD bares his holy arm before the eyes of all the nations.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.98.3.s1","verses":[3],"source":"זָ֘כַ֤ר חַסְדּ֨וֹ׀וֶֽאֱֽמוּנָתוֹ֮ לְבֵ֪ית יִשְׂרָ֫אֵ֥ל רָא֥וּ כָל־אַפְסֵי־אָ֑רֶץ אֵ֝֗ת יְשׁוּעַ֥ת אֱלֹהֵֽינוּ׃","gloss":"He has remembered his loyal love and his faithfulness to [the] house of Israel; all [the] ends of [the] earth have seen the salvation of our God.","pieces":[[3,"He has kept in mind {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} loyal love and faithfulness toward the people of Israel; \\q the farthest places on earth have seen \\q how our God saves.",null]],"L":{"3":"He has remembered {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} loyal love and {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} faithfulness to the house of Israel; \\q all the ends of the earth have seen \\q the salvation of our God."},"R":{"3":"He has not forgotten {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} faithful love for the people of Israel, and {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} has kept {{deity_pronoun:his|His}} promises to them. \\q People in the farthest places on earth have seen \\q our God save us."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190980030021"],"choice":"loyal love: chesed","alternatives":["steadfast love","kindness","mercy"],"reason":"The word (chesed) is the love that keeps faith, God's commitment to his people that does not give up (5:8).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190980030011"],"choice":"remembered: acted on what he had promised","alternatives":[],"reason":"When God \"remembers\" his love it means he acts on it, as he remembered his covenant in Egypt (Exodus 2:24).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m3","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o190980030081","o190980030121"],"choice":"Isaiah 52:10","alternatives":[],"reason":"\"All the ends of the earth will see the salvation of our God\" is the promise of Isaiah 52:10; here it is sung as done.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190980030021"],"choice":"faithful love","alternatives":["loyal love"],"reason":"As in the earlier psalms, Readable says \"faithful love\" for chesed.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190980030032"],"choice":"kept his promises","alternatives":["faithfulness"],"reason":"Readable says what God's faithfulness did.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.98.4.s1","verses":[4],"source":"הָרִ֣יעוּ לַֽ֭יהוָה כָּל־הָאָ֑רֶץ פִּצְח֖וּ וְרַנְּנ֣וּ וְזַמֵּֽרוּ׃","gloss":"Shout to YHWH, all the earth; break forth and sing for joy and make music.","pieces":[[4,"Raise a glad shout to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, all the earth; \\q burst into joyful song and make music!",null]],"L":{"4":"Shout for joy to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, all the earth; \\q break forth and sing for joy and make music."},"R":{"4":"Everyone on earth, shout happily to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}! \\q Break out in joyful singing and play music!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190980040011"],"choice":"shout: the cry that greets a king","alternatives":["shout in triumph"],"reason":"The verb (heria') is to raise a loud shout, as when a king is welcomed (Numbers 23:21; 1 Samuel 10:24).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190980040072"],"choice":"make music: sing and play","alternatives":[],"reason":"The verb (zimmer) is to make music with voice and instrument; verses 5-6 name the instruments.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.98.5.s1","verses":[5],"source":"זַמְּר֣וּ לַיהוָ֣ה בְּכִנּ֑וֹר בְּ֝כִנּ֗וֹר וְק֣וֹל זִמְרָֽה׃","gloss":"Make music to YHWH with [the] lyre, with [the] lyre and [the] sound of melody.","pieces":[[5,"Make music for {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} on the lyre, \\q the lyre and the voice of song!",null]],"L":{"5":"Make music to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} with the lyre, \\q with the lyre and the sound of song."},"R":{"5":"Play music for {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}} on the harp! \\q Play the harp and sing songs to {{deity_pronoun:him|Him}}!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o190980050032"],"choice":"lyre: a small stringed instrument","alternatives":["harp"],"reason":"The kinnor was a hand-held stringed instrument, played by David (1 Samuel 16:23).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190980050061"],"choice":"melody: song with music","alternatives":[],"reason":"The word (zimrah) is a song or tune, sung or played.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"word_choice","tokens":["o190980050032"],"choice":"harp","alternatives":["lyre"],"reason":"Readable uses the more familiar name for a stringed instrument.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-2","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o190980050061"],"choice":"to him","alternatives":[],"reason":"Readable says to whom the songs are sung.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.98.6.s1","verses":[6],"source":"בַּ֭חֲצֹ֣צְרוֹת וְק֣וֹל שׁוֹפָ֑ר הָ֝רִ֗יעוּ לִפְנֵ֤י׀הַמֶּ֬לֶךְ יְהוָֽה׃","gloss":"With trumpets and [the] sound of [the] horn shout before the King, YHWH.","pieces":[[6,"With trumpets and the ram's horn sounding, \\q lift a glad shout before the King, {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}.",null]],"L":{"6":"With trumpets and the sound of the ram's horn \\q shout for joy before the King, {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}."},"R":{"6":"Blow the trumpets and the ram's horn! \\q Shout for joy to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, the King!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o190980060012","o190980060031"],"choice":"trumpets and horn: the sounds of a king's crowning","alternatives":[],"reason":"The trumpets (chatsotserot) were metal, blown by priests (Numbers 10:2); the horn (shofar) was a ram's horn. The horn was blown when a king was crowned (1 Kings 1:39).","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190980060062","o190980060071"],"choice":"the King, the LORD","alternatives":[],"reason":"The LORD is hailed as King, the theme of Psalms 93-99.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.98.7.s1","verses":[7],"source":"יִרְעַ֣ם הַ֭יָּם וּמְלֹא֑וֹ תֵּ֝בֵ֗ל וְיֹ֣שְׁבֵי בָֽהּ׃","gloss":"Let the sea thunder and its fullness, [the] world and those who dwell in it.","pieces":[[7,"Let the sea and everything in it thunder, \\q the world and everyone living there.",null]],"L":{"7":"Let the sea thunder, and its fullness, \\q the world and those who dwell in it."},"R":{"7":"Let the sea and every creature in it roar! \\q Let the world and everyone who lives in it join in!"},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o190980070011","o190980070032"],"choice":"Psalm 96:11; 24:1","alternatives":[],"reason":"The first line repeats 96:11; \"the world and those who dwell in it\" is from 24:1.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o190980070052"],"choice":"join in","alternatives":[],"reason":"Readable repeats the verb for the second line, which the Hebrew leaves understood.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.98.8.s1","verses":[8],"source":"נְהָר֥וֹת יִמְחֲאוּ־כָ֑ף יַ֝֗חַד הָרִ֥ים יְרַנֵּֽנוּ׃","gloss":"[The] rivers — let them clap a hand; together [the] mountains — let them sing for joy","pieces":[[8,"May the rivers clap their hands, \\q and the mountains all sing for joy together,",null]],"L":{"8":"Let the rivers clap [their] hands; \\q together let the mountains sing for joy"},"R":{"8":"Let the rivers clap for joy, \\q and let all the mountains sing together."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"culture","tokens":["o190980080021","o190980080031"],"choice":"clap hands: applause for a king","alternatives":[],"reason":"Clapping greeted a new king (2 Kings 11:12; 47:2). The rivers and mountains are pictured joining the welcome, as in Isaiah 55:12.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"grammar","tokens":["o190980080061"],"choice":"a sentence that runs on","alternatives":[],"reason":"\"Before the LORD\" in verse 9 completes this line, so the verse ends with a comma at Balanced; Literal ends without a full stop.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"},{"id":"PSA.98.9.s1","verses":[9],"source":"לִֽפְֽנֵי־יְהוָ֗ה כִּ֥י בָא֮ לִשְׁפֹּ֪ט הָ֫אָ֥רֶץ יִשְׁפֹּֽט־תֵּבֵ֥ל בְּצֶ֑דֶק וְ֝עַמִּ֗ים בְּמֵישָׁרִֽים׃","gloss":"before YHWH, for he comes to judge the earth. He will judge [the] world with righteousness and [the] peoples with uprightness.","pieces":[[9,"in the presence of {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, for {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} is on the way to judge the earth. \\q He will govern the world rightly \\q and the peoples with fairness.",null]],"L":{"9":"before {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, for {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} comes to judge the earth. \\q He will judge the world with righteousness, \\q and the peoples with uprightness."},"R":{"9":"Let them sing to {{divine_name:the LORD|Yahweh}}, because {{deity_pronoun:he|He}} is coming to judge the earth. \\q He will rule the world with justice \\q and treat all people fairly."},"decisions":[{"id":"m1","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"allusion","tokens":["o190980090041","o190980090112"],"choice":"Psalm 96:13","alternatives":[],"reason":"The ending repeats 96:13 almost word for word, with \"uprightness\" in place of \"his faithfulness\".","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"m2","layer":"meaning","levels":null,"category":"word_sense","tokens":["o190980090052","o190980090071"],"choice":"judge: rule and set things right","alternatives":[],"reason":"As in 96:13, the verb (shafat) is to govern and to put wrongs right; the coming of this Judge is cause for joy.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false},{"id":"r-en-1","layer":"rendering","levels":["R"],"category":"supplied_words","tokens":["o190980090011"],"choice":"Let them sing","alternatives":[],"reason":"Readable ended verse 8 with a full stop, so it repeats the call to sing.","uncertain":false,"footnote":false}],"heading":null,"status":"ai_draft"}],"words":{"1":[{"id":"o190980010011","text":"מִזְמ֡וֹר","after":"","lemma":"מִזְמוֹר","morph":"Ncmsa","gloss":"a.psalm","strong":"4210","transliteration":"mizmôr","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine singular absolute"},{"id":"o190980010021","text":"שִׁ֤ירוּ","after":" ","lemma":"שִׁיר","morph":"Vqv2mp","gloss":"sing","strong":"7891","transliteration":"šiyrû","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Qal · imperative · 2nd person masculine plural"},{"id":"o190980010031","text":"לַֽ","after":"","lemma":"לְ","morph":"R","gloss":"to","strong":"3807a","transliteration":"la","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o190980010032","text":"יהוָ֨ה","after":"׀","lemma":"יהוה","morph":"Np","gloss":"Yahweh","strong":"3068","transliteration":"yhwāh","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · proper name"},{"id":"o190980010041","text":"שִׁ֣יר","after":" ","lemma":"שִׁיר","morph":"Ncbsa","gloss":"a.song","strong":"7892","transliteration":"šiyr","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · masculine or feminine singular absolute"},{"id":"o190980010051","text":"חָ֭דָשׁ","after":" ","lemma":"חָדָשׁ","morph":"Aamsa","gloss":"new","strong":"2319","transliteration":"ḥāḏāš","lang":"H","parse":"Adjective · masculine singular absolute"},{"id":"o190980010061","text":"כִּֽי","after":"־","lemma":"כִּי","morph":"C","gloss":"(dm)","strong":"3588","transliteration":"kiy-","lang":"H","parse":"Conjunction"},{"id":"o190980010071","text":"נִפְלָא֣וֹת","after":" ","lemma":"פָּלָא","morph":"VNrfpa","gloss":"wonders","strong":"6381","transliteration":"nip̄lāʾôṯ","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Niphal · participle · feminine plural absolute"},{"id":"o190980010081","text":"עָשָׂ֑ה","after":" ","lemma":"עָשָׂה","morph":"Vqp3ms","gloss":"he.has.done","strong":"6213","transliteration":"ʿāśāh","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Qal · perfect (qatal) · 3rd person masculine singular"},{"id":"o190980010091","text":"הוֹשִֽׁיעָה","after":"־","lemma":"יָשַׁע","morph":"Vhp3fs","gloss":"it.has.given.victory","strong":"3467","transliteration":"hôšiyʿâ-","lang":"H","parse":"Verb · Hiphil · perfect (qatal) · 3rd person feminine singular"},{"id":"o190980010101","text":"לּ֥","after":"","lemma":"לְ","morph":"R","gloss":"to","strong":"3807a","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Preposition"},{"id":"o190980010102","text":"וֹ","after":" ","lemma":"הוּא","morph":"Sp3ms","gloss":"him","strong":"2050c","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Suffix · pronoun · 3rd person masculine singular"},{"id":"o190980010111","text":"יְ֝מִינ֗","after":"","lemma":"יָמִין","morph":"Ncfsc","gloss":"hand","strong":"3225","transliteration":"","lang":"H","parse":"Noun · common · feminine singular construct (of ...)"},{"id":"o190980010112","tex